on with various internal and external stakeholders, plans and conducts on-campus events, such as recruitment and conversion events, the annual TRU Williams Lake Convocation ceremony, donor announcements, alumni events, the annual TRU Williams Lake Gala and all other institution related events. Coordinates and participates in local and targeted community events, on behalf of the TRU Williams Lake community. Monitors and assists all Faculties, Schools and Departments on the TRU Williams Lake campus in organizing events to ensure events are executed with high quality, consistency and to ensure protocols are met. Communicates with a high level of professionalism and tact within the TRU Williams Lake Campus, within TRU and outside of TRU as a key representative for the university and campus, specifically. Builds and maintains relationships with relevant on-campus and off-campus community networks. REPORTS TO Manager, Williams Lake Enrolment Services & Student Support QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION: A four-year baccalaureate degree in relevant area EXPERIENCE: Two years’ related experience in a post-secondary environment where marketing, event management, public speaking, and stakeholder engagement were part of the responsibilities. Experience in editing, written communication, social media advertising, project management software, and annual reports SKILLS, KNOWLEDGE OR ABILITIES RELATED TO THE JOB Ability to communicate effectively to culturally diverse audiences, verbally and in writing Demonstrated ability to conduct effective presentations Ability to deal courteously and tactfully with students, parents, donors, VIP’s, government officials, campus and community partners, and the general public Excellent time management and organizational skills with the ability to be results oriented and to juggle conflicting priorities while working within tight timeframes and demanding workloads Demonstrated ability to use Word, PowerPoint, Excel, Adobe Creative Suite Extensive knowledge of marketing concepts and best practices Knowledge of University academic policies, admission requirements and program information Project management skills with the proven ability to plan, lead and coordinate projects on time and on budget Detail and deadline oriented Demonstrated ability with event planning Ability to travel, independently, for extended periods of time, by road and air travel Valid Class 5 BC Driver’s license with no restrictions that would prevent incumbent from required travel Knowledge of media vendors and media buying Working knowledge of content management systems and customer relationship management systems High level of tact, discretion, and ability to handle and maintain confidential information with the ability to respond appropriately and use judgement when to refer to the Manager, Williams Lake Enrolment Services and Student Support, Associate Dean, Williams Lake and/or Designate Dean, Williams Lake WORKING CONDITIONS Sitting at a desk for long periods of time Travel required within Canada Ability to lift and load up to 25kg Standing for long periods of time on concrete floors during events and education fairs Work outside in all types of weather Flexibility in work hours, some evening and weekend work required General office conditions The salary for the above position is determined by the Collective Agreement with the Canadian Union of Public Employees, Local 4879, as it presently exists. Pay Band $32.54 - $36.16 ( CUPE Grade 08 (90% - 100%) ) Salary rate This Position is not subject to a 90% start rate for new Employees. Location Williams Lake, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Williams Lake Campus -> Operations, Williams Lake Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job"
