    "https://tru.hua.hrsmart.com/hr/ats/Posting/view/35517": {
      "title": "Medical Office Assistant - Auxiliary/On Call - (00152.25)",
      "description": "Jump to main content Attention Safari users: This site requires cookies to function. Please click here to accept the cookie. Cookies will be used strictly for the functioning of the site. Toggle navigation Job Search View All Jobs Create Account Log in Help Help on this Page Job Details Medical Office Assistant - Auxiliary/On Call - (00152.25) Share this job as a link in your status update to LinkedIn. Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Support Staff (CUPE) Posting In effect from 22/9/2026 Closing Application Date 7/10/2026 Closing date for internal CUPE applicants Applications will be reviewed commencing the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” and may continue until the position is filled. Internal CUPE applicants must submit their application by 4pm on the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” for their Seniority to be recognized. Applications received after the \"closing date for internal CUPE applicants\" will be considered alongside external applicants. Full/Part Time Part Time Support Type Auxiliary (Under 4 Months) Anticipated Start Date 13/10/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) The Hours of work are subject to change depending upon departmental requirements Schedule Varied Schedule Description Coverage shifts as needed, may be full days or partial days depending on need DUTIES Thompson Rivers University (TRU) seeks qualified individuals for our Medical Office Assistant Auxiliary/On Call pool.  The Auxiliary/On Call pool of employees provides temporary, short-term support to designated departments within the University to assist with workload requirements, temporary leave coverage and during peak periods. The length of an Auxiliary assignment can vary from one day to up to four months and can be part-time or full-time hours depending on the departmental requirements. Provides a wide variety of confidential clerical and medical office assistant duties including:  reception, billing, screening, assisting patients and, under direction, arranges appointments with other health care professionals.  Assists the Campus Physician with routine clinical procedures according to established protocols. MAJOR DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES Performs clinical administrative duties such as reception by screening and assisting patients to ensure correct and appropriate information is either acquired or provided; arranges patient appointments for health care professionals such as physician(s), psychologist(s), psychiatrist(s), and community health nurse(s); processes departmental mail to ensure efficient and effective flow of information. Provides occasional clerical assistance and support to the Safety Officer and Associate Director S&EM. Responsible for billing WCB, ICBC, MSP and private insurance companies. Coordinates the flu clinics by arranging student/staff appointments, ordering all supplies and scheduling of community-based nurses or other health practitioners to administer flu shots. Compiles related confidential records, ministry and other reports, statistics and charts by performing such duties as filing/retrieving patient records. Processes confidential medical documentation of students entering programs with medical prerequisites. Arranges appointments and liaises with health agencies, medical specialists, x-rays, laboratory or hospital. As a member of the Health Care Team provides clerical support to assist with coordination of programs designed to promote health awareness within the TRU population. As directed, assists the Campus Physician with clinical procedures such as sterilization of medical tools/equipment and prepares equipment for use, prepares specimens for transport and prepares patients prior to examination according to established guidelines and protocols. Performs and records confidential routine tests such as pregnancy, urine, blood pressure and vision; takes and records patient's weight and height as required. Reconciles weekly cash reports and forwards to the Finance department. Cleans and tidies the First Aid room and Examination rooms. Responsible for ordering and maintaining office and medical supplies. Coordinates the work of work-study students. Locates Students in event of emergency situations. REPORTS TO Associate Director, Safety & Emergency Management QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION: Grade 12 plus a Medical Office Assistant Certificate or equivalent EXPERIENCE: Two years related experience in a physician's office, community medical clinic or a hospital medical clerical unit SKILLS, KNOWLEDGE OR ABILITIES RELATED TO THE JOB Ability to perform word processing at 45 wpm Ability to maintain a standard of absolute confidentiality regarding medical information and records Ability to deal courteously with students, staff and members of the medical community and general public Ability to operate office equipment such as copier, printer and fax machine Practical working knowledge of routine patient care treatments WORKING CONDITIONS Working in close proximity to patients and Health Centre staff Front counter work and working at computer for long periods of time Ability to lift weights up to 10 kg. The salary for the above position is determined by the Collective Agreement with the Canadian Union of Public Employees, Local 4879, as it presently exists. Pay Band $30.98 - $34.42 ( CUPE Grade 07 (90% - 100%) ) Salary rate Please Note: This position may be subject to a 90% salary for the first 560 hours of employment. Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Student Services -> AVP,  Students -> Medical Clinic Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job v18.5.4 Last sync: 2026-09-24 03:55:04 Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Support Staff (CUPE) Posting In effect from 22/9/2026 Closing Application Date 7/10/2026 Closing date for internal CUPE applicants Applications will be reviewed commencing the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” and may continue until the position is filled. Internal CUPE applicants must submit their application by 4pm on the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” for their Seniority to be recognized. Applications received after the \"closing date for internal CUPE applicants\" will be considered alongside external applicants. Full/Part Time Part Time Support Type Auxiliary (Under 4 Months) Anticipated Start Date 13/10/2026 Position End Date (If Applicable) The Hours of work are subject to change depending upon departmental requirements Schedule Varied Schedule Description Coverage shifts as needed, may be full days or partial days depending on need DUTIES Thompson Rivers University (TRU) seeks qualified individuals for our Medical Office Assistant Auxiliary/On Call pool.  The Auxiliary/On Call pool of employees provides temporary, short-term support to designated departments within the University to assist with workload requirements, temporary leave coverage and during peak periods. The length of an Auxiliary assignment can vary from one day to up to four months and can be part-time or full-time hours depending on the departmental requirements. Provides a wide variety of confidential clerical and medical office assistant duties including:  reception, billing, screening, assisting patients and, under direction, arranges appointments with other health care professionals.  Assists the Campus Physician with routine clinical procedures according to established protocols. MAJOR DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES Performs clinical administrative duties such as reception by screening and assisting patients to ensure correct and appropriate information is either acquired or provided; arranges patient appointments for health care professionals such as physician(s), psychologist(s), psychiatrist(s), and community health nurse(s); processes departmental mail to ensure efficient and effective flow of information. Provides occasional clerical assistance and support to the Safety Officer and Associate Director S&EM. Responsible for billing WCB, ICBC, MSP and private insurance companies. Coordinates the flu clinics by arranging student/staff appointments, ordering all supplies and scheduling of community-based nurses or other health practitioners to administer flu shots. Compiles related confidential records, ministry and other reports, statistics and charts by performing such duties as filing/retrieving patient records. Processes confidential medical documentation of students entering programs with medical prerequisites. Arranges appointments and liaises with health agencies, medical specialists, x-rays, laboratory or hospital. As a member of the Health Care Team provides clerical support to assist with coordination of programs designed to promote health awareness within the TRU population. As directed, assists the Campus Physician with clinical procedures such as sterilization of medical tools/equipment and prepares equipment for use, prepares specimens for transport and prepares patients prior to examination according to established guidelines and protocols. Performs and records confidential routine tests such as pregnancy, urine, blood pressure and vision; takes and records patient's weight and height as required. Reconciles weekly cash reports and forwards to the Finance department. Cleans and tidies the First Aid room and Examination rooms. Responsible for ordering and maintaining office and medical supplies. Coordinates the work of work-study students. Locates Students in event of emergency situations. REPORTS TO Associate Director, Safety & Emergency Management QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION: Grade 12 plus a Medical Office Assistant Certificate or equivalent EXPERIENCE: Two years related experience in a physician's office, community medical clinic or a hospital medical clerical unit SKILLS, KNOWLEDGE OR ABILITIES RELATED TO THE JOB Ability to perform word processing at 45 wpm Ability to maintain a standard of absolute confidentiality regarding medical information and records Ability to deal courteously with students, staff and members of the medical community and general public Ability to operate office equipment such as copier, printer and fax machine Practical working knowledge of routine patient care treatments WORKING CONDITIONS Working in close proximity to patients and Health Centre staff Front counter work and working at computer for long periods of time Ability to lift weights up to 10 kg. The salary for the above position is determined by the Collective Agreement with the Canadian Union of Public Employees, Local 4879, as it presently exists. Pay Band $30.98 - $34.42 ( CUPE Grade 07 (90% - 100%) ) Salary rate Please Note: This position may be subject to a 90% salary for the first 560 hours of employment. Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> Student Services -> AVP,  Students -> Medical Clinic Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job"
