that accompany this understanding. Students will work with families and individuals in the home and community, in agencies, and in care facilities to incorporate concepts and learning from all the courses in this semester into their nursing practice. The community and society are considered as contextual influences on the promotion of health for the individual and the family. Section Site Schedule Dates Comments Credits P01 Practice - Surg (GT8) Tues/Wed 0730-1430 March 9 - April 14 + 1 week for evals Practice hours 84.5 4.5 P02 Practice - Surg (5N) Tues/Wed 0730-1430 Jan 12 - Feb 24 + 1 week for evals Practice hours 84.5 4.5 P02 Practice – MH (GT6) Tues/ wed 0730-1430 March 9 – April 14 + 1 week for evals Practice hours 84.5 4.5 P03 Practice – MAT/ SIM Tues/ wed 0730-1430 Jan 12 – Feb 24 + 1 week for evals Practice hours: 84.5. Mix of practice on GT3 and sim 4.5 P03 Practice – Surg (5N) Tues/ wed 0730-1430 March 9 – April 14 + 1 week for evals Practice hours 84.5 4.5 P04 Practice – HH Tues/ wed 0730-1430 Jan 12 – Feb 24 + 1 week for evals Practice hours 84.5 4.5 P04 Practice – Med (GT7) Tues/ wed 0730-1430 March 9 – April 14 + 1 week for evals Practice hours 84.5 4.5 P06 Practice – MAT/SIM Tues/ wed 0730-1430 March 9 – April 14 + 1 week for evals Practice hours: 84.5. Mix of practice on GT3 and sim 4.5 P07 Practice – MH (GT6) Thurs/ Fri 0730 - 1430 Jan 14 – Feb 26     +1 week for evals Practice hours 84.5 4.5 P08 Practice – Med (GT7) Thurs/ Fri 0730 - 1430 Jan 14 – Feb 26     +1 week for evals Practice hours 84.5 4.5 P08 Practice – MH (GT6) Thurs/ Fri 0730 - 1430 March 11 – April 16 + 1 week for evals Practice hours 84.5 4.5 P11 Practice – MH (Hillside) Thurs/ Fri 0730 - 1430 March 11 – April 16 + 1 week for evals Practice hours 84.5 4.5 P12 Practice – MH (Hillside) Thurs/ Fri 0730 - 1430 Jan 14 – Feb 26     +1 week for evals Practice hours 84.5 4.5 QUALIFICATIONS Master's degree required; Holds a Bachelor's degree in Nursing; Three (3) years of full-time or equiva