oftware applications. Liaises with the supervisor and other TRU Departments to assist with program planning and delivery. In coordination with other team members, supports programs and workshops by collaborating on deliverables, ensuring materials are available, and coordinating shared equipment. Prepares and maintains course setup, class lists, course reconciliations, and course completion requirements. Secures sufficient facilities, and ensures supplies and resources are available for course delivery and instructors within current TRU procedures. Prepares a variety of documents including correspondence, contracts, evaluation summaries, curriculum preparation, and memos. Maintains the department database of statistical course information, instructors, contract agencies, and stakeholders. Sets up and maintains filing systems (paper and electronic). Assists with financial reporting including tracking expenses and providing financial updates on course deliveries. Also makes travel arrangements for instructors to travel to various communities. Maintains the web page, and social media accounts and assists with online and pprint advertising. REPORTS TO Community Coordinator QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION: Grade 12 plus a one-year Business certificate or equivalent EXPERIENCE: Two years’ related experience, including one years’ experience in program delivery and one years’ experience with Microsoft office and website software SKILLS, KNOWLEDGE OR ABILITIES RELATED TO THE JOB Ability to perform electronic word processing at 60 wpm and data entry Ability to deal courteously and tactfully with students, staff and members of the general public Ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing Ability to operate related equipment Must be fluent in database, desktop publishing, spreadsheet, and word processing software Proven ability to work independently as well as part of a team Ability to plan, organize, and prioritize tasks and meet deadlines while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail Class 5 driver’s license WORKING CONDITIONS Sitting at a desk and computer for a period of time Extensive contact with students, staff, and the general public General office conditions Travel required The salary for the above position is determined by the Collective Agreement with the Canadian Union of Public Employees, Local 4879, as it presently exists. Pay Band $29.60 - $32.89 ( CUPE Grade 06 (90% - 100%) ) Salary rate Please Note: This position may be subject to a 90% salary for the first 560 hours of employment. Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires Needed 1 Organizational Unit Thompson Rivers University -> School of Trades and Technology -> Trades, Continuing Studies Diversity and Inclusion Commitment: Thompson Rivers University is strongly committed to hiring based on merit with a focus on fostering diversity of thought within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, Indigenous, Black and People of Colour, persons with disabilities and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply, however applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. NOTE: To learn more about Thompson Rivers University or living in Kamloops or Williams Lake please visit our Careers website . External Candidates invited to interview will be required to bring a copy of their transcripts to the interview. Apply to this Job v18.5.5 Last sync: 2026-10-30 00:50:03 Application Restrictions Open to both Internal and external Job Type Support Staff (CUPE) Posting In effect from 29/10/2026 Closing Application Date 13/11/2026 Closing date for internal CUPE applicants 13/11/2026 Applications will be reviewed commencing the “closing date for internal CUPE applicants” and may continue until the position is filled. Internal CUPE applicants must